GermanQuAD retrieval uses annotations by deepset (CC BY 4.0) and passages from
German Wikipedia (CC BY-SA). The pinned MTEB exports supply queries, corpus and
relevance judgments.
https://huggingface.co/datasets/mteb/germanquad-retrieval
https://huggingface.co/datasets/mteb/germanquad-retrieval-qrels

FineWeb-2 by Hugging Face supplies German distractors (ODC-By 1.0, also subject
to the Common Crawl terms of use). The test takes the first 5,000 nonempty texts
from the pinned shard and caps each text at 6,144 characters.
https://huggingface.co/datasets/HuggingFaceFW/fineweb-2

QASPER by the Allen Institute for AI supplies the English evaluation set
(CC BY 4.0). The preparer uses test abstracts and body paragraphs and maps
questions to evidence paragraphs by whitespace-normalized exact matches.
https://huggingface.co/datasets/allenai/qasper

See manifest.json for revisions, exact payload URLs and SHA-256 values.
